('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_6','infantile paralysis','','','小儿麻痹','I had got infantile paralysis since I was four years old. The disease had been torturing me. My heart sank.  四岁起，我就患了小儿麻痹症，忍受著病魔的摧残折磨，弱小的心灵笼罩著可怕的阴影。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_7','Rosalyn','','','[n] 罗莎琳（女名）','While studying the chemistry of human body , Dr. Rosalyn Yalow won a Nobel Prize for the research she conducted on the role of hormones .  罗莎琳，雅罗博士在研究人体化学组成的过程中，因为荷尔蒙的作用所进行的研究而获得了一项诺贝尔奖。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_8','lap','læp','læp','[n] （人坐着时）大腿的上方；跑道的一圈','Shannon sat on her mother’s lap.  香农坐在她妈妈的腿上。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_9','ambition','æm''bɪʃən','æm''bɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 雄心；野心','He was young and full of ambition.  他年轻，而且雄心勃勃。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_10','ambitious','æm''bɪʃəs','æm''bɪʃəs','[adj] 有雄心的；有野心的','Alfred was intensely ambitious, obsessed with the idea of becoming rich.  艾尔弗雷德雄心勃勃，一心想着发财。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_11','dictation','dɪk''teʃən','dɪk''teɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 口授；听写（的文字）','There were no secretaries available to take dictation (= write down what someone is saying ) .  身边没有秘书记录口授内容。'),
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO words (book_slug, slug, word, phonetic_us, phonetic_uk, meaning, example) VALUES,
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_12','Sally','''sæli','''sælɪ','[n] 萨利（女名）','Felicity (to Sally): I guess what I’m saying is this might all be a colossal mistake, as my dad would say, but on the other hand it may…maybe it’ll save my life or something.  费利西蒂(对莎莉说): 我猜我想要说的这个可能是个巨大的错误，如同我爸爸说的那样，但是另一方面也许……也许它可拯救我的生命或者别的什么。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_13','noisy','ˈnɔɪzɪ','ˈnɔɪzɪ','[n] 吵闹的；嘈杂的','The kids have been really noisy today.  孩子们今天实在是吵。'),
('PEPGaoZhong_7','PEPGaoZhong_7_14','suitable','''sutəbl','''suːtəb(ə)l','[adj] 适合的；适宜的','We are hoping to find a suitable school.  我们希望能找到一所合适的学校。'),
