('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1623','lamp','læmp','læmp','[n] 灯；照射器; [vt] 照亮; [vi] 发亮','She switched on the bedside lamp.  她打开了床头灯。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1624','shopkeeper','''ʃɑp''kipɚ','''ʃɒpkiːpə','[n] 店主，老板','The girl had only worked for the shopkeeper for three days when she packed him in.  这姑娘替那店主只干了三天， 就辞职不干了。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1625','holiday','''hɑləde','''hɒlɪdeɪ; -dɪ','[n] 假日；节日；休息日; [v] 外出度假','The school holidays start tomorrow.  学校假期从明天开始。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1626','fact','fækt','fækt','[n] 事实；实际；真相','Our decision to build the museum in Hartlepool was influenced by the fact that there were no national museums in the North East.  我们之所以决定在哈特尔浦建造博物馆，是因为东北地区没有国家级的博物馆。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1627','extra','''ɛkstrə','''ekstrə','[adv] 特别地，非常；另外; [n] 临时演员；号外；额外的事物；上等产品; [adj] 额外的，另外收费的；特大的','They need to offer something extra to attract customers.  他们需要提供额外的东西以吸引顾客。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1628','indicate','''ɪndɪket','''ɪndɪkeɪt','[v] 表明；指出；预示；象征','The study indicates a connection between poverty and crime.  研究显示贫穷和犯罪有关联。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1629','frantic','''fræntɪk','''fræntɪk','[adj] 狂乱的，疯狂的','I spent three frantic days trying to get everything ready.  我花了三天时间手忙脚乱地做准备。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1630','overcoat','''ovɚkot','''əʊvəkəʊt','[n] 大衣，外套','I sprang 400 pounds for  her overcoat.  给她买那件大衣，我花了400镑。'),
