('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1652','crimson','''krɪmzn','''krɪmz(ə)n','[n] 深红色; [adj] 深红色的; [v] 使变为深红色；脸红','Smith said the crimson anthocyanin protects the delicate mechanisms that allow the tree to extract all the nutrients from its leaves.  史密斯说，深红色的花青素保护着微妙的机制，它让树木从叶子里提取所需要的全部营养物。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1653','enigmatic','''ɛnɪg''mætɪk',',enɪg''mætɪk','[adj] 神秘的；高深莫测的；谜一般的','She starred in one of Welles''s most enigmatic films.  她主演了威尔斯最神秘的电影当中的一部。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1654','harry','''hæri','''hærɪ','[v] 折磨；掠夺；骚扰；使苦恼; [n] (Harry)人名；(英)哈里，哈丽(女名)(教名Henry、Harriet的昵称)','He is increasingly active in harrying the government in late-night debates.  他愈来愈积极地在午夜辩论节目中不断攻击政府。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1655','bored','bɔrd','bɔːd','[adj] 无聊的；无趣的；烦人的; [v] 使厌烦（bore的过去式）；烦扰','He was easily bored.  他很容易感到厌烦。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1656','purport','''pɝpɔt','pə''pɔːt','[v] 声称；意图；意指；打算; [n] 意义，主旨；意图','...a book that purports to tell the whole truth.  …一本声称讲出全部真相的书。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1657','estimable','''ɛstɪməbl','''estɪməb(ə)l','[adj] 可估计的；可尊敬的；有价值的','...the estimable Miss Cartwright.  ...令人仰慕的卡特赖特小姐。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1658','firecracker','''faɪɚkrækɚ','''faɪəkrækə','[n] 鞭炮，爆竹','I played firecracker but I hurt my finger with the fire.  在我玩爆竹的时候，伤着了我的手指。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1659','deodorant','dɪ''odərənt','dɪ''əʊd(ə)r(ə)nt','[adj] 除臭的；防臭的; [n] 除臭剂','But in 2002, researchers at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle conducted a study to address this rumor—and found no link between deodorant or antiperspirant and breast cancer.  在2002年，西雅图的费雷德哈钦森癌症中心进行了一项研究，该研究结果表明除臭剂或止汗剂与乳腺癌没有关系，从而澄清了这一谣言。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1660','flatter','''flætɚ','''flætə','[v] 奉承；谄媚；使高兴','Perry would always flatter Mrs. Mitchell by praising her cooking.  佩里常常奉承米切尔太太，称赞她的烹调手艺。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1661','punishment','''pʌnɪʃmənt','''pʌnɪʃm(ə)nt','[n] 惩罚；严厉对待，虐待','...a group that campaigns against the physical punishment of children.  …一个发起运动反对体罚儿童的组织。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1662','orchard','''ɔrtʃɚd','''ɔːtʃəd','[n] 果园；果树林','a cherry orchard  樱桃园'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1663','grassroots','''græs''rʊts','''gra:s,ru:ts','[adj] 基层的；草根的；乡村的; [n] 草根；基础','Actually, it does not have to do this while there are enough grassroots on sand for them to survive through dry season.   其实，沙鼠不用往自己的洞里叼，沙地上的草根足以使它们度过旱季的，可沙鼠们不这样做便焦虑不安。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1664','interjection',',ɪntɚ''dʒɛkʃən','ɪntə''dʒekʃ(ə)n','[n] [语] 感叹词；插入语；突然的发声','...the moronic and insensitive interjections of the disc jockey.  ...该音乐主持人愚蠢而迟钝的插话。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1665','incursion','ɪn''kɝʒn','ɪn''kɜːʃ(ə)n','[n] 入侵；侵犯','...armed incursions into border areas by rebel forces.  ...叛军武装入侵边境地区。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1666','purchase','''pɝtʃəs','''pɜ:tʃəs','[n] 购买；紧握；起重装置; [v] 购买；赢得','She paid for her purchases and left.  她付钱买好东西离开了。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1667','possibility',',pɑsə''bɪləti',',pɒsɪ''bɪlɪtɪ','[n] 可能性；可能发生的事物','There’s always a possibility that he might go back to Seattle.  他也许会回到西雅图去，这种可能性一直存在。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1668','possibly','''pɑsəbli','''pɒsɪblɪ','[adv] 可能地；也许；大概','This last task is possibly the most difficult.  这最后一项任务也许是最难的。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1669','sweatshop','''swɛtʃɑp','''swetʃɒp','[n] 血汗工厂；剥削劳力的工厂','Her boy has never been to a doctor or a dentist, and last bathed when he was 2, so a sweatshop job by comparison would be far more pleasant and less dangerous.  他的儿子从来没看过医生或者牙医，最后一次洗澡是在2岁的时候，所以两相对照，血汗工厂的工作将会开心的并且没有那么危险。'),
('Level8luan_2','Level8luan_2_1670','perch','pɝtʃ','pɜːtʃ','[n] 鲈鱼; 高位；栖木；杆; [v] 栖息；就位；位于；使坐落于','She watched the parade from her perch on her father’s shoulders.  她骑在父亲的肩上观看游行。'),
